<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    RUT_Sump - FROZEN, carrying the world until the terminal paint; content
    lives in mandrake.rm.thesump; do not edit here.

    THESUMP_RM_MOD_BUILD_1 (Phase A, 2026-09-25): this def is unchanged below,
    byte-for-byte, except this header. The standalone franchise-free sibling,
    RM_TheSump, now lives in src/RimMandrake/TheSump/Defs/BiomeDefs/
    RM_TheSump_Biome.xml, carrying the same content (its own RM_BiomeWorker_TheSump
    replacing the donor AlphaBiomes.BiomeWorker_TarPits, plus AA_BumbledroneQueen
    added to wildAnimals per the roster, and RSW_Hssiss riding a Utinni patch
    instead of inline). The kit content this BiomeDef's own modExtensions/the
    separate wiring patch reference (RUT_SumpWeather, RUT_SumpDuskLock +
    its BiomeWiring patch, RUT_TarMoat/RUT_TarSpent, RUT_MoatFusePost,
    RUT_BeastBulge + its GenStep/Register/DreadRegistration, RUT_DigShaft,
    RUT_DigStratumTable, RUT_Filth_MouseTrack, RUT_Placeholder_SumpMouseRace/
    RUT_Placeholder_SumpMouse, RUT_ThinkTree_SumpMouseWander, RUT_Plant_Wick,
    RUT_WickStem) moved with their defNames UNCHANGED into mandrake.rm.thesump's
    own Defs/ and Patches/ trees — this def's own references below (RUT_Tarred
    via the shared EnvironmentalHazards modExtension, and the dusk lock wired
    externally) keep resolving exactly as before, since RUT_SumpDuskLock/
    RUT_SumpWeather are read by BOTH biome instances under the same defNames.
    RUT_Tarred (the hediff) and its surgery/solvents/thoughts content, plus the
    newer Walkways/Bitumen/Sumpgas/Gaslight kit content (SUMP_WALKWAYS_1,
    SUMP_TAR_NASTINESS_1, SUMP_GASLIGHT_1, all 2026-09-24), are NOT biome-gated
    and were left in UtinniPatches — not this pass's scope to relocate; the
    Sumpgas rename and flame-statue ideoligion meaning are explicitly
    SUMP_UTINNI_LAYER_1's campaign-tier work, not this mod's.

    ORIGINAL HEADER, preserved below for provenance:

    RUT_Sump                                       UtinniPatches - authored 2026-09-09
    BIOME_OWNERSHIP_WAVE_1. Full sheet: design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/the_sump.md
    (FROZEN). Replaces the donor `AB_TarPits` (Alpha Biomes). THE TAR'S ORIGIN IS
    RULED (SS0, R-H9): the Pyrelands make the tar, drainage carries it nightward,
    and the Sump — lowest ground on the planet — is where it collects.

    MEASURED (sheet SS0): 42 tiles just past the terminator on the night side, sun
    median -10.6 deg (permanent deep twilight), temp p10/median/p90 -4.3/1.2/14.9 C,
    elevation median 1 m, dead flat.

    animalDensity/plantDensity CORRECTED from the donor (sheet SS0): "corrected —
    animalDensity 3.5 drops to sparse-but-strange; plantDensity 0.25 fits the
    edge-ring pattern" — no exact replacement figure is given in the sheet, so 1.0
    / 0.15 are DESIGNED interim values (same pattern as RUT_TheScald/RUT_GreySea),
    lower than the donor's own numbers per the sheet's explicit "drops"/"sparse"
    language, with a quicktest tune still owed.

    Weather: ban 4 ("No rain, no surface water defs — the only liquid is tar") zeros
    Rain/RainyThunderstorm/FoggyRain. Ban 5 ("No warm-climate donor flavor — 'sun-
    baked' and its kin are stripped") is why Fog (not Clear) carries the baseline:
    "permanent deep twilight... the sun a glow below the horizon" (SS1/SS9) reads as
    fog-dim, not desert-clear; the donor's own sun-baked-mud framing is dropped
    entirely, matching SS0's "corrected" note. SnowGentle/SnowHard kept modest (the
    donor's own values, cold-night-appropriate at -4..15 C).

    wildAnimals/wildPlants: transplanted from BiomeCast_Ashkarr.xml /
    BiomeFlora_Ashkarr.xml against rosters/the_sump.json. Ban 2 (no tar beast as a
    fightable spawn — set-piece only) means the tar beasts are NOT in this
    wildAnimals list; they are a separate dormant-set-piece mechanic (SS4, SS Owed).

    NOT this pass's scope: `SUMP_MECHANICS_1` (poured-moat buildable, dig-lottery
    tables, tar beast set-piece logic, mouse-line telegraphy); wick-garden crop; any
    world repaint.

    UPDATED — SUMP_MECHANICS_1 S6 build pass: <modExtensions> below carries
    BiomeGlowMultiplierExtension (ALPHA_MECHANICS_KIT_1, ruled/shipped), glowMultiplier
    0.55 per sump_kit_spec.md S6's own INVENTED value ("deep dusk, darker than Miasma's
    0.85, lighter than a cave"). MayRequire is on the <li> itself, not the whole
    BiomeDef (per infrastructure memory modextension-missing-type-discards-def: an
    unresolvable Class inside <modExtensions> drops the WHOLE containing def unless the
    <li> is individually gated) — this file must always load regardless of whether
    mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards is active. The permanent-dusk weather lock
    (RUT_SumpDuskLock) is wired separately via
    Patches/RUT_SumpDuskLock_BiomeWiring.xml — a plain <li> defName reference in
    biomeMapConditions WOULD be a dangling cross-reference if that mod were absent,
    unlike a modExtensions Class, so it needs the patch route instead; see that file's
    own header. ❓ live glow-multiplier calibration against the frozen tile's actual
    sun-dot value is still owed (no-bridge scope this pass, per SUMP_MECHANICS_1's own
    spike-pass S6 finding: the multiplier only affects the fractional residual glow
    band, and whether the frozen Sump tile ever falls in that band isn't checkable
    offline).

  -->

  <BiomeDef>
    <defName>RUT_Sump</defName>
    <label>the Sump</label>
    <description>The planet's oil sump: the lowest basin on Ash'karr, filled by every slow black flow off the twilight slopes for geological time. Flat black pools and cooled glassy sheets under permanent dusk, ringed with low waxy plants that glow faintly where the Junker stations keep their lamp-gardens. Mice run the tar without a thought. Nothing else touches it -- because the tar takes slowly, keeps perfectly, and everything that ever blundered in is still in there.</description>
    <workerClass>AlphaBiomes.BiomeWorker_TarPits</workerClass>

    <allowRoads>true</allowRoads>
    <allowRivers>true</allowRivers>
    <allowFarmingCamps>true</allowFarmingCamps>
    <animalDensity>1.0</animalDensity>
    <plantDensity>0.15</plantDensity>
    <forageability>0.0</forageability>
    <movementDifficulty>4</movementDifficulty>
    <texture>Biomes/AB_TarPits</texture>
    <diseaseMtbDays>65</diseaseMtbDays>
    <diseases>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_Flu</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_Plague</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_GutWorms</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>60</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_MuscleParasites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>60</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_FibrousMechanites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>30</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_SensoryMechanites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>30</commonality>
      </li>
    </diseases>
    <terrainsByFertility>
      <li>
        <terrain>AB_GrassySand</terrain>
        <min>-999</min>
        <max>0.25</max>
      </li>
      <li>
        <terrain>AB_LushGrass</terrain>
        <min>0.25</min>
        <max>999</max>
      </li>
    </terrainsByFertility>
    <baseWeatherCommonalities>
      <Fog>50</Fog>
      <Clear>15</Clear>
      <DryThunderstorm>1</DryThunderstorm>
      <Rain>0</Rain>
      <RainyThunderstorm>0</RainyThunderstorm>
      <FoggyRain>0</FoggyRain>
      <SnowGentle>2</SnowGentle>
      <SnowHard>2</SnowHard>
    </baseWeatherCommonalities>
    <wildAnimals>
      <AA_TarGuzzler MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.5</AA_TarGuzzler>  <!-- tar guzzler - tar-eater, adjust-keep -->
      <AA_Bumbledrone MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.35</AA_Bumbledrone>  <!-- bumbledrone - under-layer, keep -->
      <AA_BumbledroneHierophant MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.2</AA_BumbledroneHierophant>  <!-- bumbledrone hierophant - under-layer, keep -->
    </wildAnimals>
    <coastalWildAnimals />
    <wildPlants>
      <AB_TarPuddle>0.6</AB_TarPuddle>  <!-- tar puddle -->
    </wildPlants>
    <wildPlantRegrowDays>20</wildPlantRegrowDays>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.BiomeGlowMultiplierExtension" MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">
        <glowMultiplier>0.55</glowMultiplier>
        <suppressSunlightStatAffecter>true</suppressSunlightStatAffecter>
      </li>
      <!-- SUMP_TAR_NASTINESS_1 (2026-09-24, item spec §2): the giver half of
           the tarred-pawn mechanic. RM_MapComponent_CarriedFilthHediffLink
           reads this off map.Biome every scan; presence is the opt-in, same
           idiom BiomeGlowMultiplierExtension above already uses. MayRequire
           on the <li> itself, not the whole BiomeDef, for the same reason
           that entry's own header already documents — this def must always
           load regardless of whether mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards is
           active. -->
      <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_CarriedFilthHediffExtension" MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">
        <filthDef>RM_Filth_Tar</filthDef>
        <hediffDef>RUT_Tarred</hediffDef>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </BiomeDef>

</Defs>
